sequenceDiagram

actor Admin
participant Server as server.js
participant Route as routes/admin.js + guards + validation
participant C as controllers/providerLifecycle.js
participant S as services/bookings.js
participant M as Provider / ProviderApplication / User + native collections
participant DB as MongoDB
Admin->>Server: POST /api/v1/admin/providers/{providerId}/suspend
Server->>Route: Parsed JSON
Route->>C: Admin actor, validated providerId and reason
activate C
C->>DB: Start transaction
C->>M: Increment Provider revision guard
M->>DB: Lock provider in session
C->>M: Require approved Provider and approved application
M->>DB: Read approved application in same session
C->>M: Save suspended status, reason, time and admin
M->>DB: Provider save in same session
C->>S: cancelNonCompletedForProvider with active session
activate S
S->>M: Find confirmed bookings with dueDate at/after Thailand today
M->>DB: Native bookings collection read in session
loop Distinct user IDs in sorted order
    S->>M: Increment User.bookingRevision
    M->>DB: Lock user in same session
end
loop Distinct vehicle IDs in sorted order
    S->>M: Increment vehicle revision
    M->>DB: Lock vehicle in same session
end
S->>M: Cancel matching bookings with provider_suspended reason
M->>DB: Native updateMany in same session
S-->>C: Actual cancelledBookingCount
deactivate S
DB-->>C: Commit suspension and cancellations together
C->>C: Serialize provider and count
C-->>Server: 200 success
deactivate C
Server-->>Admin: JSON result
Note over C,DB: Any failure aborts both changes, matching provider-first guards serialize booking writes
Note over Server,DB: Protected provider requests check current status, this operation does not revoke AuthSession records
